validateAllowlist
├── when enforcement is disabled
│   ├── it should accept a single non-allowlisted user
│   ├── it should accept a non-allowlisted caller and beneficiary
│   └── it should accept identical non-allowlisted addresses
└── when enforcement is enabled
    ├── when a single user is not allowlisted
    │   └── it should revert with that user
    ├── when a single user is allowlisted
    │   └── it should succeed, including arbitrary and zero addresses
    ├── when the caller is not allowlisted
    │   └── it should revert with the caller, even if the beneficiary is also not allowlisted
    ├── when only the beneficiary is not allowlisted
    │   └── it should revert with the beneficiary, including the zero address
    ├── when both addresses are allowlisted
    │   └── it should succeed, including a zero beneficiary
    ├── when both addresses are identical
    │   ├── it should succeed if allowlisted
    │   └── it should revert if not allowlisted
    └── it should not change enforcement or membership
